 "notes": "Derived edit. developed_at (the lab) and developed_at_site (the town of the work) are local. Premise 3 ('Bell Labs developed Unix at its Murray Hill headquarters') is stored as 'at its headquarters', a rule, so in w2 the site moves with the headquarters. The site-in-state rule is firm, and so is the record's bridge 'Unix was originally developed in only one US state' (one_dev_state). Since 2026-10-31 each world adds only the side facts it names, with placeholders (a site or headquarters town in some state), never Massachusetts: the site-in-state rule and one_dev_state derive it. The earlier firm 'one state per place' rule (one_state) is gone: no answer needs it. Relations once declared in this file are catalogued in RELATIONS.md since 2026-10-30.",
